# Enforce consistent line endings regardless of local core.autocrlf.
#
# Root cause of issue #258: husky/claude hook shell scripts broke on
# Linux/macOS when checked out with core.autocrlf=true, because git's
# smudge filter injected CRLF into them (the committed blobs were, and
# remain, clean LF). .gitattributes makes this repo-enforced instead of
# depending on each contributor's local git config.

# Default: treat everything git considers text as LF, let git auto-detect binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly pin all shell scripts to LF; these are executed directly by
# bash and break with "bad interpreter"/syntax errors under CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
.claude/hooks/* text eol=lf

# Known binary types: never touch, no diff noise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
